course: dictionary
lesson: 7781
title: Pyramid: a shape, a pile, a tomb
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: One word can have more than one meaning, and the sentence tells you which one to use. Look at the clues around the word. «The Great Sphinx is a huge statue with a lion's body and a pharaoh's head, carved from the rock next to the pyramids» tells you the pyramids are huge old buildings, so this is the building meaning.
explain: Pyramid can also be a shape. In maths, a pyramid has a flat bottom called the base, and sides shaped like triangles that meet at a point at the top. Check your meaning by swapping it into the sentence. If the sentence is about shapes, faces or edges, the shape meaning fits.
explain: Pyramid can also mean a pile of things in rows that get smaller towards the top, like a food pyramid in science. A food pyramid shows which foods you should eat most. If the words around the word talk about rows, foods or getting smaller, this is the meaning you need. Read the whole sentence before you decide.
fact: A pyramid has a flat base and sides shaped like triangles that meet at a point at the top.
fact: A square pyramid has 5 faces: one square base and four triangles.
fact: «Pyramids» in Egypt are huge old stone buildings, made as tombs for kings.
fact: «Cleopatra lived about 2,000 years ago, so in her time the Great Pyramid was already about 2,500 years old.»
fact: A food pyramid shows which foods to eat most, with the rows getting smaller towards the top.
exercise: «The Great Sphinx is a huge statue ... next to the pyramids.» In this sentence, what are the pyramids? | A kind of statue with a lion's body | *Huge old stone buildings | A pile of things in rows that get smaller
exercise: How many faces does a square pyramid have? | 4 | *5 | 6 | 8
exercise: In a food pyramid, what do the rows show? | The number of tombs in Egypt | *Which foods to eat most | The faces of a square pyramid | A kind of statue
test: What is the flat bottom of a pyramid called? | Its tip | *Its base | Its face | Its edge
test: In the sentence about Cleopatra, what was already about 2,500 years old when she lived? | Chichen Itza | Wrangel Island | *The Great Pyramid | Cleopatra
exam: Jayden sees «a pile of boxes in rows, smaller at the top» and says it is a pyramid. Which meaning is he using? | *A pile of things in rows that get smaller towards the top | A statue with a lion's body | A tomb for a king | A solid shape with a flat base and triangle sides
